WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:05.060
Bohemian Rhapsody will rock you — or at
least Rami Malek's performance in the film

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.560
will.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.940
20th Century Fox screened Bohemian Rhapsody,
the musical drama biopic centered on the legendary

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.759
rock band Queen and it's even more iconic
frontman, Freddie Mercury, for press and critics

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:18.440
on Sunday, October 7th in Los Angeles.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.220
Those in attendance have since shared online
their first reactions to the film.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:22.960
The verdict?

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.900
Bohemian Rhapsody is largely enjoyable, if
not pretty cookie-cutter as far as biopics

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.400
go.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.440
And while IndieWire's Anne Thompson expects
the film to "get mixed reviews," it appears

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.760
everyone agrees that Malek's turn as Freddie
Mercury is a dazzling sight to behold.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.640
Many - even Kyle Buchanan of The New York
Times, who called the film a "glorified Wikipedia

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.560
entry" - have praised Malek's performance
as being out-of-this-world incredible.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.019
In fact, they're already placing bets on Malek
receiving an Oscar nomination for Best Actor

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:50.880
for his work.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.720
Us Weekly film critic Mara Reinstein tweeted,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.400
"How do you turn an OK movie into a good one?

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.780
Five words: Rami Malek as Freddie Mercury.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.820
#BohemianRhapsody."

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.540
Jenna Busch, the founder and editor in chief
of Legion of Leia, was also completely swept

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.460
away, tweeting,

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.940
"Absolutely beyond blown away by [Bohemian
Rhapsody]!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.500
Rami Malek is phenomenal.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.880
Gorgeous story, amazing concert movie…

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.300
I don't have enough words!"

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.440
More unabashed praise came from film critic
Scott Mantz, who exclaimed,

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.540
"HOLY HELL!!

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.090
[Bohemian Rhapsody] is ABSOLUTELY FANTASTIC!!

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.100
A rousing emotional cinematic champion that
will rock you!

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.000
[Rami Malek] is magnificent!

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.750
It's great FUN &amp; it will ROCK YOU!!

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.840
A Star Is Born, you've been served!!"

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.760
In the eyes of many critics, Malek went above
and beyond in his interpretation of Mercury.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.880
"You don't want to mimic Freddy.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.500
You want to be able to understand why he did
what he did."

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.820
Playing a real-life figure is never an easy
task for actors - no matter how much they

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.400
look like the people they portray.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.490
For Malek, stepping into Mercury's shoes meant
more than just putting on an accent, rocking

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:57.080
eccentric costumes, and wearing false teeth
that gave him Mercury's famous overbite.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.960
"You can pop em in and pop em out, but I chose
to keep them in for the majority of the shoot...Really,

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.560
even at lunch...No."

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.550
According to Entertainment Weekly, Malek practiced
singing Queen songs every night while wearing

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:14.290
the fake chompers before Fox even greenlit
Bohemian Rhapsody, and pored over Mercury's

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.250
past interviews and performances.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.950
The actor even took a trip to London - financed
entirely out of pocket before Bohemian Rhapsody

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.520
had even received funding - to conduct research.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:29.010
Malek met with Queen drummer Roger Taylor
and lead guitarist Brian May, dug into biographies,

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.700
and watched old footage of Mercury.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.460
Additionally, Malek worked with movement coach
Polly Bennett to capture Mercury's unique

00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:40.260
physicality, and collaborated with choreographers
ahead of filming to ensure he was as prepared

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.140
as he could be.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.439
Speaking to Vanity Fair, Malek shared that
Bennett would have him, quote, "do ludicrous

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:50.849
things like ski across the room," in efforts
to mimic Mercury's signature on-stage theatrics.

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:53.959
Malek essentially studied every little thing
Mercury did.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.540
He explained,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.099
“I watched the way his lips moved while
he was singing, and everything that’s happening

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.700
in his throat and his vocal cords.”

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.600
Sounds like all that hard work paid off.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:06.120
Once Fox lifts the review embargo a few days
ahead of the film's release, some opinions

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:08.670
about Bohemian Rhapsody are sure to change.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.250
For now, though, the initial responses are
promising.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.629
Decide for yourself whether Bohemian Rhapsody
is a killer queen or a just a bunch of radio

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:18.260
ga-ga when the movie debuts on November 2nd.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.620
"Alright!"

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:20.960
"Alright!"

